# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 🔐 SECURE ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 
# This is a TEMPLATE file. Copy it to .env.local and add your actual values.
# NEVER commit .env.local to git!
#
# Setup instructions:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.local.example .env.local
# 2. Replace placeholder values with your actual API keys
# 3. Restart the development server: npm run dev
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenAI API Key (Required for AI features)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get your key from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#
# Security notes:
# - Keys start with 'sk-proj-' or 'sk-'
# - Never share your API key publicly
# - Rotate keys immediately if exposed
# - Set usage limits in your OpenAI dashboard
#
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_ACTUAL_KEY
